  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section id="faq" class="py-20 px-6 bg-bg-secondary">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary mb-8">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <details class="bg-white rounded-card shadow-card overflow-hidden group">
          <summary class="px-6 py-4 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-primary text-sm flex items-center justify-between">
            What is an expert network?
            <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 flex-shrink-0"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-4 text-sm text-secondary">An expert network is a service that connects professionals who need specialized knowledge (investors, consultants, corporate strategists) with subject-matter experts for paid consultations, surveys, and research projects. The industry was founded in 1998 by GLG and now includes 33+ providers we track.</div>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-white rounded-card shadow-card overflow-hidden group">
          <summary class="px-6 py-4 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-primary text-sm flex items-center justify-between">
            How much does an expert network cost?
            <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 flex-shrink-0"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-4 text-sm text-secondary">Pricing varies significantly. Expert calls typically range from $500 to $1,800+ per hour depending on expert seniority and the network. Some providers use per-call pricing, others use credit-based subscriptions, and some offer flexible mixed models. See our <a href="/expert-network-pricing" class="text-accent hover:underline">complete pricing guide</a>.</div>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-white rounded-card shadow-card overflow-hidden group">
          <summary class="px-6 py-4 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-primary text-sm flex items-center justify-between">
            Are expert networks legal?
            <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 flex-shrink-0"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-4 text-sm text-secondary">Yes, expert networks are entirely legal. They operate under strict compliance frameworks designed to prevent the exchange of material non-public information (MNPI). After SEC enforcement actions in 2010–2016, the industry substantially strengthened its compliance infrastructure. Reputable providers have expert vetting, conflict screening, call monitoring, and audit trails.</div>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-white rounded-card shadow-card overflow-hidden group">
          <summary class="px-6 py-4 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-primary text-sm flex items-center justify-between">
            Who uses expert networks?
            <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 flex-shrink-0"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-4 text-sm text-secondary">Private equity firms, hedge funds, venture capital firms, management consultancies, investment banks, corporate strategy teams, and law firms. Anyone who needs to make high-stakes decisions informed by real industry expertise rather than desk research alone.</div>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-white rounded-card shadow-card overflow-hidden group">
          <summary class="px-6 py-4 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-primary text-sm flex items-center justify-between">
            What's the difference between GLG and AlphaSights?
            <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 flex-shrink-0"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-4 text-sm text-secondary">GLG is the industry pioneer (1998) with the broadest product suite and ~1.2M experts. AlphaSights (2008) is a faster-growing challenger known for speed and custom-sourcing. GLG is stronger in breadth and multi-format research; AlphaSights is known for high-touch service and rapid delivery. See our <a href="/glg-vs-alphasights" class="text-accent hover:underline">detailed comparison</a>.</div>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-white rounded-card shadow-card overflow-hidden group">
          <summary class="px-6 py-4 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-primary text-sm flex items-center justify-between">
            How do I become an expert on an expert network?
            <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 flex-shrink-0"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-4 text-sm text-secondary">Most networks recruit experts directly based on specific project needs. You can also apply through provider websites. Compensation for experts typically ranges from $200–$500+/hr depending on seniority and specialization. Networks look for professionals with deep, current industry knowledge in specific verticals.</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
